  "meta": {
    "title": "Act 2 — Sea: The Brine Reach",
    "note": "The five main quests of Act 2 (game-story.md §4, issue #144). Act 2 is PART OF THE OPEN WORLD — decided in review of the zone-based first cut of #227: seaward of Embervale's coastline the landform blends into an island sea (terrain.ts SEA_DIR/SEA_START/SEA_FULL), island towns stand past it, and the deep water that refuses you on foot is the act gate. There is no `brine` zone and never will be.",
    "loading": "Boot-loaded (see bootstrapContent in main.ts): the islands physically exist from frame 1 because the world is one world, so their settlements must exist when planSettlements runs. What `sea-revealed` opens is the FERRY — the means of crossing — not the geography. The flag-gated loading recorded in issue #209 was a zone-era decision and went with the zone.",
    "the-stub": "Nothing is stubbed any more (#152): `npc:gain/saltrest` stands in the harbour with the act's opening talk rows, and the quest names its giver and its triggers. He is the SECOND PLACEMENT of the Encampment's Gain (game-story.md §2): one `body` factory, one display-name key, and the joke that he is always already there when you arrive."
  },
